Revision history for Log-Munger

0.1.0   ????-??-??/??:??
        - openvpn: gate on ovpn-<instance> (Debian openvpn@.service)
        - sendmail: gate on sm-acceptingconnections
        - fail2ban: gate on fail2ban-server and accept its logger prefix,
          captured as f2b_logger
        - dovecot: match passdb failures from auth-worker, the 2.3 worker
          conn chain, and the newer auth(user,rip)<...> prefix
        - dovecot: add "Login aborted ... (code)" and prose-reason
          disconnects (submission-login)
        - dovecot: Aborted login no longer requires user=
        - dovecot: optional level on login lines (log_path output)
        - dovecot: split a trailing TLS error out of dovecot_kv as
          dovecot_tls_state / dovecot_tls_error
        - dovecot: auth failure lines now capture dovecot_service
        - exim: accept log_selector +pid prefix and I=, Ci=, X=, CV=, SNI=
          after the peer
        - exim: reject accepts unbracketed F=/recipient, "rejected after
          DATA" and a leading message id
        - exim: connect ACL "dropped by" form, captured as exim_acl_action
        - exim: add no MAIL, SMTP protocol error, synchronization error,
          sender/recipient verify fail, reverse/forward DNS lookup failures,
          local_scan() rejects and SA-Exim SA: Action lines
        - asterisk: prefix accepts older forms (no line/function, no "in",
          no colon after thread id), dialplan Log() lines and the
          full/messages file timestamp
        - asterisk: security events take the last LocalAddress and
          RemoteAddress, so a forged one injected via a client-supplied
          field no longer sets asterisk_src_ip
        - asterisk: Request failed accepts no method and quotes in From
        - asterisk: add chan_sip registration failure, extension not found,
          IAX2 and AMI auth failures, hacking attempt, and FreePBX unknown
          SIP connection
        - sshd: usernames may contain spaces and the last " from <ip>" wins,
          so a forged address in the username no longer sets ssh_src_ip;
          same for the Bad protocol identifier
        - sshd: port optional on Failed, Connection closed and disconnects
        - sshd: Received disconnect captures ssh_disconnect_code and
          ssh_disconnect_reason, and takes an error: prefix
        - sshd: User ... not allowed takes a hostname (UseDNS), PAM errors
          take " via <ip>"
        - sshd: old "Disconnecting: Too many authentication failures" form,
          fatal: prefix on Unable to negotiate
        - sshd: add Disconnecting <state> user, ssh_dispatch_run_fatal,
          ROOT LOGIN REFUSED, tcp_wrappers refused connect and a catch-all
          for error:/fatal: lines with no function name
        - postfix: smtpd reject matches milter-reject and a syslog-truncated
          line with no "; from=... to=..." tail
        - postfix: improper command pipelining no longer needs trailing data
        - postfix: add too many errors after, anvil rate/concurrency limit
          warnings and hostname does not resolve warnings, each capturing
          the client address
        - mysql: accept the MySQL 5.5 YYMMDD date, MariaDB space-padded hour
          and a prefix with no thread id
        - openvpn: client-instance restarting (SIGUSR1) matched, captured as
          openvpn_client_instance; the signal name may contain digits
        - openvpn: add tls-auth/tls-crypt "TLS Error: ... from [AF]ip:port"
          and "TLS Auth Error" username/password failures
        - vsftpd: [pid N] optional (syslog_enable=YES), ::ffff: mapped
          client addresses unwrapped, FAIL LOGIN refusal reason captured as
          vsftpd_reason
        - pam: match the pre-0.99 "(pam_unix) " and "pam_unix: " prefixes and
          a bare "authentication failure; logname=..." line
        - dovecot: login lines take the last rip=/lip= pair, so a pair forged
          in user=<> no longer sets dovecot_rip
        - dovecot: passdb account is greedy, so an address planted after a
          comma in it no longer sets dovecot_rip
        - dovecot: managesieve "bytes=in/out" session stats
        - vsftpd: FAIL LOGIN takes the last Client marker, so one forged in
          the typed account no longer sets vsftpd_client_ip
        - pam: ruser/rhost/user read as fail2ban reads them (789571aa), so a
          rhost= forged in ruser no longer sets pam_rhost and a ruser with a
          space no longer drops the bare form
        - sendmail: relay= captured by the patterns, so one forged in an
          address or in user= no longer sets sendmail_relay_ip; a ruleset line
          whose arg1 holds a space or comma yields no relay at all
        - sendmail: ruleset lines split by key, reject= kept whole
        - sendmail: AUTH failure takes a queue id, captured user as
          sendmail_user
        - sendmail: [IPv6:addr] relays, host before "did not issue"
        - sendmail: add possible SMTP attack, pre-greeting traffic, EXPN/VRFY
          rejected, lost input channel and "<rcpt>... status" lines
        - http_access_logs: quoted fields take apache's \" escapes, so a quote
          in the user agent no longer fails the line
        - http_access_logs: nginx main's x-forwarded-for, Traefik's request
          count/router/backend/duration, and anything else after the agent
          (http_extra) are taken instead of failing the line
        - http_access_logs: %u takes any account basic auth sent, spaces
          included; methods may hold a hyphen; a request path with spaces
          keeps its verb/path/version when the line ends in HTTP/x
        - http_error_logs: apache "ErrorLog syslog" lines read by a second rule
          gated on httpd/apache2
        - http_error_logs: nginx tail takes login, subrequest, upstream and
          referrer; a line holding a second ", client: " tail, or a client-set
          value with a space, yields no address rather than a forged one
        - http_error_logs: apache 2.4 [client] takes bracketed and unbracketed
          IPv6 and ::ffff: mapped addresses, [remote] captured as
          http_error_remote_ip, [pid] optional, ModSecurity's second [client]
          skipped, http_error_code only AHnnnnn, ", referer:" split out
        - http_error_logs: apache 2.2 [client] takes a port
        - http_error_logs: add lighttpd and suhosin; auth failures name the
          account as http_error_user
        - named: client lines take BIND's own timestamp, print-category and
          print-severity prefixes (dns_category, dns_severity) and a
          "view <name>: " (dns_view)
        - named: add zone transfer denied, bad zone transfer request (NOTAUTH)
          and update / update forwarding denied
        - named: gate accepts named-<variant> (named-pkcs11, named-sdb)
        - proftpd: head takes the older "): " form, ::ffff: mapped client
          addresses unwrapped
        - proftpd: refusals with no "(Login failed)" (no such user found,
          Limit access denies login, Invalid shell, ...) captured with user
          and reason; accounts may hold spaces
        - fail2ban: add Repeal Ban, Reban and Increase Ban
        - fail2ban: a comma may follow the address (Found <ip>, bad ...;
          Ignore <ip>, expired bantime); subnet bans give f2b_prefixlen, an id
          that is no address goes to f2b_id
        - fail2ban: leading timestamp (logtarget=STDOUT) as f2b_time, level as
          f2b_level; jail names may hold spaces
        - dropbear: older lowercase wordings, the journal's "[pid] date "
          prefix, a missing port, and ::ffff: mapped peers unwrapped
        - dropbear: usernames greedy, so a "' from <addr>" forged in one no
          longer sets dropbear_src_ip
        - dropbear: older "Exit before auth (user ...): ... from <peer>" form;
          user and fail count captured as dropbear_user / dropbear_fails
        - haproxy: captured request/response header blocks before the request
          taken as haproxy_req_headers / haproxy_res_headers instead of
          failing the line; ::ffff: mapped client addresses unwrapped
        - mongodb: 4.4's attr.client split into mongo_attr_client_ip/_port and
          looked up, as attr.remote is
        - mongodb: pre-4.4 text log (2.6 and 3.x) read into the JSON field
          names: auth failures, connection accepted / end connection, and the
          rest as mongo_msg
        - mongodb: peer split tries ip:port first, so an unbracketed v6 peer
          keeps its port
        - slapd: ACCEPT takes bracketed v6 peers and listeners (IP=[::]:389),
          ::ffff: mapped peers unwrapped, and ldapi PATH= sockets
          (slapd_src_path / slapd_dst_path)
        - slapd: add TLS established; RESULT of an extended operation (empty
          oid=, no tag=)
        - convert: add hex (aliases unhex, hexdecode), decoding whole hex
          bytes and passing anything else through
        - auditd: USER_ERR read by the USER_* pattern
        - auditd: a hex-encoded (unquoted) acct= or cmd= decoded into
          audit_msg_acct_decoded / audit_msg_cmd_decoded
        - auditd: log_format = ENRICHED's values after the \x1D separator
          taken as audit_enriched and split into audit_UID, audit_AUID, ...

0.0.1   2026-08-23/17:00
        - init
